{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHyGtFs9GUVBEa6TkV1YC8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd013-true\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n6\t  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n7\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n8\t  coreutils) in exit code behavior, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, ignoring all arguments.\n12\t  - G2: Produce no output unless --help or --version is given.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Core behavior\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments, ignoring them entirely. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: Must not read from stdin. Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n24\t\n25\t  R2:\n26\t    title: Help and version output\n27\t    items:\n28\t      - R2.1:\n29\t          text: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0.\n30\t      - R2.2:\n31\t          text: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0.\n32\t      - R2.3:\n33\t          text: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output, must exit 1.\n34\t\n35\t  R3:\n36\t    title: Exit codes\n37\t    items:\n38\t      - R3.1:\n39\t          text: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n40\t      - R3.2:\n41\t          text: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n42\t\n43\t  R4:\n44\t    title: Differential testing\n45\t    items:\n46\t      - R4.1:\n47\t          text: Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n48\t      - R4.2:\n49\t          text: \"Tests must cover: no arguments, arbitrary arguments (ignored), --help output, and --version output.\"\n50\t      - R4.3:\n51\t          text: Tests must verify that no output is produced on stdout or stderr when invoked without --help or --version.\n52\t\n53\tnon_goals:\n54\t  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n55\t  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n56\t\n57\tacceptance_criteria:\n58\t  - id: AC1\n59\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R1.1\n62\t      - R1.2\n63\t      - R1.3\n64\t  - id: AC2\n65\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n66\t    traces:\n67\t      - R1.1\n68\t      - R1.2\n69\t      - R1.3\n70\t  - id: AC3\n71\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message and exits 0, matching gtrue --help.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R2.1\n76\t      - R2.2\n77\t      - R2.3\n78\t      - R3.1\n79\t      - R3.2\n80\t      - R4.1\n81\t      - R4.2\n82\t      - R4.3\n83\t  - id: AC4\n84\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtrue passes for no-args and arbitrary-args cases.\"\n85\t    traces:\n86\t      - R4.1\n87\t  - id: AC5\n88\t    criterion: \"cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R1.1\n91\t      - R1.2\n92\t      - R1.3\n93\t      - R2.1\n94\t      - R2.2\n95\t      - R2.3\n96\t      - R3.1\n97\t      - R3.2\n98\t      - R4.1\n99\t      - R4.2\n100\t      - R4.3\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb04f38f-6fb0-484d-ab16-7faefa8d0057","uuid":"90185ae2-fe8f-445c-b378-f24e733e9ed4","timestamp":"2026-05-14T02:30:35.159Z","tool