t compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: no arguments, arbitrary arguments (ignored), --help output, and --version output.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that no output is produced on stdout or stderr when invoked without --help or --version.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message and exits 0, matching gtrue --help.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtrue passes for no-args and arbitrary-args cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
